  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Spanish Pipedream (Jim solo) (John Prine song, only one verse played)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Death Is The Easy Way (Jim solo)**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2002-03-21.aud.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 15 songs; 76 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Band headlined again; monitor trouble on and off, soundman struggled to give them the sound they wanted; crowd was chatty until someone shushed them [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2002-03-21.aud.flac16**: taped by George \"Low Dog\" S.; transferred by Magnix; source: AUD MD > CD-R [1]. Also: Transferred from CD-R through EAC to FLAC level 8, part of the Magnix archive, volume 29; Recording came from Low Dog, who taped the band while effectively on tour with them, passed along directly [1]",
